From 2582d40dd25700327893f03b70c31d004a70573f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:58:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] agent: close git.exec sandbox escapes; watches,
 conditional writes, deflate, git.spawn

Security (all reachable under --git-exec-preset read-only before this):
- refuse denied long options in every spelling git accepts (unambiguous
  abbreviations, separate-argument values, bundled short options):
  grep -O/--open-files-in-pager and ls-remote --upload-pack/--exec ran
  commands; --output wrote files; diff with outside paths, blame
  --contents, grep -f read files outside the roots
- read-only preset no longer creates branches/tags; config, branch, tag,
  symbolic-ref are served in their read forms only
- repoPath is authorized against the roots
- the git child no longer inherits the RPC channel as its stdin

Function (each of these sent the client down its slow fallback path):
- rev-parse --git-dir, subcommand-level -c/-C, config and the plumbing
  magit uses are served; stdinBase64 and env (GIT_INDEX_FILE...) carried

Performance:
- fs.listDirectory {watch}: inotify-backed fs.changed notifications,
  ordered before the reply to the request that caused them
- fs.writeFile {ifMtimeNs}: compare-and-swap save; result carries entry
- maxEntries / maxBytes refusals; mtimeNs everywhere; hello carries
  roots, home, config state and a feature list
- zlib deflate of large responses and tunnel output (rpc.deflate)
- git.spawn / git.signal: asynchronous git as a tunnel, with exit by
  waitpid, own process group, credential broker; tunnelSend {eof}
- tunnels: finished commands are freed; a full stdin queue can no
  longer wedge the reader thread; pipes are close-on-exec from birth

